In the above code snippets, we used Python to read the Python code and extract the comments that start with "@@@".

In the first snippet, if we have to create assert statements, we can say that the sum of the "frm" accounts' balance should not be less than the transferred amount. So we wrote, "\_\_assert\_\_ total_balance >= amnt". 

In the second snippet, we have a function which is used to transfer funds. A transfer is attempted if the sum of the "frm" accounts' balance is greater than or equal to the transferred amount. The total_balance of "frm" accounts' balance is gathered by adding up all the account balances. Therefore, we wrote, "\_\_assert\_\_ total_balance >= amnt".--------------------